.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH RANMA-LUA 1 "" "ranma 0.1.0" "ranma manual"
.SH NAME
ranma\-lua \- Evaluate Lua in the running ranma\*(Aqs configuration and print what it returns: \fBranma lua \*(Aqranma.state()\*(Aq\fR. The code is the arguments joined by spaces, or stdin when there are none. It runs as a bind does
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBranma lua\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fICODE\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Evaluate Lua in the running ranma\*(Aqs configuration and print what it returns: \fBranma lua \*(Aqranma.state()\*(Aq\fR. The code is the arguments joined by spaces, or stdin when there are none. It runs as a bind does
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fICODE\fR]
The Lua code; stdin when there is none
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBranma\fR(1)
